--[[
================================================================================
 PROJECT ZERO - Blox Fruits Structure Extractor   v2.0
================================================================================

 Read-only, metadata-only snapshot of the CLIENT-ACCESSIBLE game structure.
 It never reads Script / LocalScript / ModuleScript .Source (hard-blocked below).

 WHAT'S NEW vs v1.2
   * Streams one record per instance to a .jsonl file (no giant in-memory JSON,
     no crashes on 200k+ instance games) and yields so the client doesn't freeze.
   * Waits for the game to load + settle before scanning.
   * Stable fingerprints: volatile data (health, GUI tweens, unanchored part
     positions, playing sounds...) is excluded and numbers are rounded, so a
     fingerprint only changes when the game ACTUALLY changes.
     (v1 hashed positions/health, so every run looked "changed"; its FNV hash
     also lost precision above 2^53.)
   * Hierarchical Tree.txt with repeated siblings collapsed.
   * Update diff: automatically compares against your previous run for the same
     PlaceId and writes Diff.txt (added / removed / changed, grouped by top-most
     container, plus class-count deltas).
   * Analyzers: class histogram, largest containers, attribute names, enemy /
     NPC groups, spawn points, map islands (position + size), GUI list, remotes
     grouped by container, asset IDs (meshes, textures, sounds, animations).
   * Scope control: skips other players' characters, Terrain/Camera internals,
     only scans the LOCAL player under Players. Warns if StreamingEnabled makes
     the snapshot position-dependent.
   * Unique paths (duplicate sibling names get ~2, ~3 ...) so keys never collide.
   * One folder per run:  ProjectZero_Extractor/Run_<UTC>_P<PlaceId>/

 OUTPUT (per run folder)
   Summary.txt      human-readable overview + warnings + diff headline
   Snapshot.json    compact structured summary (analyzers, counts, remotes...)
   Instances.jsonl  one JSON object per instance (full detail, grep-friendly)
   Tree.txt         indented hierarchy (collapsed)
   Scripts.txt      script / module manifest (no source)
   Remotes.txt      remotes + bindables grouped by container
   Tags.txt         CollectionService tags
   Assets.txt       asset IDs and where they are used
   Index.tsv        key / parent / class / hash   (used for the next diff)
   Diff.txt         changes since the previous run (when one exists)

 Edit CONFIG below to tune. Defaults are tuned for Blox Fruits.
================================================================================
]]

